                  <button type="button" class="cl-fulcrum__btn is-active" data-balance-pick="living" aria-pressed="true">Living equilibrium</button>
                  <button type="button" class="cl-fulcrum__btn" data-balance-pick="hoarding" aria-pressed="false">Over-accumulation</button>
                </div>
                <svg viewBox="0 0 480 124" fill="none" role="img" aria-label="Balance beam showing equilibrium between security and living">
                  <polygon points="240,88 224,116 256,116" fill="#122026" />
                  <g class="cl-fulcrum__beam">
                    <line x1="60" y1="88" x2="420" y2="88" stroke="#122026" stroke-width="2.2" />
                    <circle cx="76" cy="70" r="14" stroke="#1b5368" stroke-width="1.5" fill="rgba(27,83,104,0.12)" />
                    <circle cx="404" cy="70" r="14" stroke="#3a6158" stroke-width="1.5" fill="rgba(58,97,88,0.12)" />
                    <text x="76" y="46" text-anchor="middle" fill="#122026" font-family="ClearMono, monospace" font-size="9">SECURITY</text>
                    <text x="404" y="46" text-anchor="middle" fill="#122026" font-family="ClearMono, monospace" font-size="9">LIVING &amp; TIME</text>
                  </g>
                </svg>
                <p class="cl-fulcrum__note" data-balance-note aria-live="polite">
                  Living equilibrium: responsibilities and future shocks are protected while time, energy, and curiosity remain free to participate in life right now.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cl-enough__copy">
              <p>
                I don't want an arbitrary number to become my only destination. I want to know what the resources are actually for.
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Enough isn't a universal amount.</strong> It's a changing balance: when accumulating more may contribute less to genuine security and possibility than the time, attention, freedom, or experiences it costs.
              </p>
              <p class="cl-enough__subtle">
                That doesn't make security optional. My responsibilities, real expenses, and future needs remain part of the answer. I can protect tomorrow without permanently postponing today.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ── NON-LINEAR RETURNING PROCESS ────────────────────────────────── -->
      <section class="cl-process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
        <div class="ph-shell">
          <p class="ph-mono cl-index">NO FINAL FORM / ONGOING</p>
          <h2 class="cl-h2" id="process-title" style="margin-top:16px">
            A process I can<br /><em>keep returning to.</em>
          </h2>
          <div class="cl-cadence" aria-label="An ongoing, non-linear cycle">
            {clearCadence.map((step, idx) => (
              <>
                {idx > 0 && <span class="cl-cadence__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↝</span>}
                <span class="cl-cadence__step">
                  <small>{String(idx + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</small>
                  {step}
                </span>
              </>
            ))}
            <span class="cl-cadence__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↺</span>
          </div>
          <p class="cl-process__copy">
            Sometimes I follow curiosity into a new skill. Sometimes I build something from it.
            Sometimes I rest, play, or simply appreciate what is already here. None of that needs to be preparation for a future version of living.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ── THIS IS HOW I SEE (#perspective) ────────────────────────────── -->
      <section class="cl-perspective" id="perspective" aria-labelledby="perspective-title">
        <div class="ph-shell cl-split">
          <p class="ph-mono cl-index">THE PERSPECTIVE / STILL EVOLVING</p>
          <div>
            <h2 class="cl-h2" id="perspective-title">
              This is how<br /><em>I see.</em>
            </h2>
            <div class="cl-perspective__copy">
              <p>
                I'm not here to wake anyone up, tell people what to believe, or hand out a formula for life.
                I want a place to express what I notice, what I question, what I make, and how my understanding changes.
              </p>
              <p>I don't need a final version of myself. I want to remain able to become.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ── FIVE WRITTEN MODELS & LENSES ────────────────────────────────── -->
      <section class="cl-models-band" aria-labelledby="models-band-title">
        <div class="ph-shell">
          <p class="ph-mono cl-index">WRITTEN MODELS &amp; LENSES / M-01 — M-05</p>
          <h2 class="cl-h2" id="models-band-title" style="margin-top:14px">
            How I check<br /><em>my own perception.</em>
          </h2>
          <div class="cl-models-grid">
            {writtenModels.map((model) => (
              <a class="cl-model-tile" href={model.href}>
                <div class="cl-model-tile__top">
                  <span>{model.idx} · {model.domain}</span>
                  <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
                </div>
                <div class="cl-model-tile__glyph">
                  <ModelGlyph slug={model.slug} accent={model.accent} />
                </div>
                <h3>{model.title}</h3>
                <p>{model.line}</p>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ── COMPANION PORTAL: GENERATIVE REALITY ────────────────────────── -->
      <section class="cl-companion" aria-labelledby="companion-title">
        <div class="ph-shell cl-companion__grid">
          <div>
            <p class="ph-mono cl-index" style="color:var(--ph-gold)">COMPANION FRAMEWORK / HOW I SEE MORE</p>
            <h2 class="cl-h2" id="companion-title" style="margin-top:14px">
              Generative<br /><em>Reality.</em>
            </h2>
            <p class="cl-companion__copy">
              Sometimes I discover an opening that was already there. Sometimes acting on that discovery builds a crossing and changes what actually becomes possible.
            </p>
            <div class="cl-companion__stages" aria-label="Six connected processes">
              {generativeStages.map((st, idx) => (
                <span>{idx > 0 ? '→ ' : ''}{st.title}</span>
              ))}
            </div>
            <a class="cl-companion__cta" href="/generative-reality.html">
              Experience the six 3D transitions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>

          <a class="cl-companion__plate" href="/generative-reality.html" aria-label="Enter Generative Reality — six spatial transitions">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 270" fill="none" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto">
              <rect width="460" height="270" fill="#071016" />
              <polygon points="16,204 176,204 176,254 16,254" fill="#17242c" stroke="#537582" stroke-opacity="0.45" />
              <polygon points="292,190 444,190 444,254 292,254" fill="#1a2c35" stroke="#537582" stroke-opacity="0.45" />
              <rect x="94" y="88" width="46" height="116" fill="#1f313b" stroke="#7ea5b0" stroke-opacity="0.55" />
              <rect x="110" y="130" width="16" height="74" fill="#071016" stroke="#e4ba75" stroke-width="1.6" />
              <polygon points="126,130 228,194 202,212 126,204" fill="rgba(228,186,117,0.22)" />
              <path d="M176,202 Q234,142 292,190" stroke="#9dcfe4" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
              <polygon points="174,202 294,188 294,198 174,212" fill="#354e59" stroke="#e4ba75" stroke-width="1.5" />
              <path d="M352,190 Q396,138 446,118" stroke="#a8d5c2" stroke-width="1.8" />
              <path d="M352,190 Q404,166 446,158" stroke="#e4ba75" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
              <text x="18" y="26" fill="#e4ba75" font-family="ClearMono, monospace" font-size="9" letter-spacing="1.5">ONE WORLD · SIX TRANSITIONS</text>
              <text x="442" y="26" text-anchor="end" fill="#a8d5c2" font-family="ClearMono, monospace" font-size="9" letter-spacing="1.5">ENTER ↗</text>
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <PhilosophyFooter active="clear" />

    <script is:inline type="application/json" data-cl-elements-json set:html={JSON.stringify(clearElements).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')} />
    <script src="../scripts/clear-essay.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
